    "ls|LS16_S10_U_106": " \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF PERSONNEL, PUBLIC GRIEVANCES AND PENSIONS \n(DEPARTMENT OF ADMINISTRATIVE REFORMS AND PUBLIC GRIEVANCE) \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 106 \n(TO BE ANSWERED ON 16.11.2016) \n \nQUALITY COUNCIL OF INDIA \n \n106. SHRI JOSE K. MANI: \n \nWill the PRIME MINISTER be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government has asked  Quality Council of India to suggest  structural \nchanges in top 20 grievance -prone ministries to address the root cause of  grievances \nreceived from the public and if so, the details thereof; \n \n(b)  whether the Quality Council has observed that the Railways, Telecom, Department of \nFinancial Services and  CBDT remain the most complaint -prone departments of the \nCentral Government; and \n \n(c)  if so, the steps being taken by the  Government to strengthen the grievance  redressal \nmechanism in these departments? \nANSWER \n \nMinister of State in the Ministry of Personnel, Public Grievances and Pensions and Minister \nof State in the Prime Minister’s Office. (DR. JITENDRA SINGH) \n(a):    Yes, Madam. Government has entrusted Quality Council of India (QCI) to conduct an \nanalysis of the grievances received in Centralized Public Grievance Redress and Monitoring \nSystem (CPGRAMS) relating to 20 Ministries/Departments /Organizations. Key issues have \nbeen identified department-wise for initiating systemic reforms. \n(b):    The QCI Study for the period 1 st January, 2012 to 19 th August, 2015 has identified \nRailways, Telecom, Department of Financial Services and CBDT as amon g the top few \nDepartments receiving large number of grievances. \n(c):    The Grievance Analysis Reports have been duly circulated to the concerned \nMinistries/Departments/Organizations including Railways, CBDT, Telecom and Financial \nServices and grievance di sposal is being regularly monitored. Respective Departments have \ntaken up reforms like automatic refund on cancellation of tickets, single window pension \nthrough disbursing banks, intensive mechanized cleaning of coaches, e-verification of income \ntax returns, expeditious income tax refunds up to 50,000/- among other reforms. \n \n***** ",
    "ls|LS16_S10_U_107": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nDEPARTMENT OF ATOMIC ENERGY \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 107 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 16.11.2016 \n \nNUCLEAR POWER POLICY \n \n107. SHRI MUTHAMSETTI SRINIVASA RAO (AVANTHI): \n SHRI CH. MALLA REDDY:  \n \nWill the PRIME MINISTER be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has framed a policy for setting up nuclear power \nplants and if so, the details thereof alongwith the  number  of plants set up so \nfar, State-wise; \n  \n(b) whether the Department of Atomic Energy (DAE) p roposes to set up nuclear \nplants in Andhra Pradesh and if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) whether the Planning Commission's Integrated En ergy Policy Study of 2006 \ndid not recommend imports of nuclear reactor exceed ing 6000 MW, if so, the \nbasis thereof; \n \n(d) whether DAE is going to import 60,000 MW nuclea r reactors and if so, the \ndetails thereof; and \n \n(e) whether reactors and fuel would be procured fro m external sources and if so, \nthe details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR PERSONNEL, PUBLIC GRIEVAN CES & \nPENSIONS AND PRIME MINISTER’S OFFICE (Dr. JITENDRA SINGH): \n \n(a) The Atomic Energy Act 1962 empowers the Governm ent to produce, develop, \nuse and dispose of atomic energy either by itself o r through any authority or \nCorporation established by it or a Government compa ny. In this regard, an \nindigenous sequential three-stage nuclear power pro gramme based on \noptimum utilization of the country’s nuclear resources of modest uranium and \nabundant thorium is being pursued. Large capacity n uclear power reactors \nbased on foreign cooperation are also being impleme nted as additionalities, \nfor faster capacity addition. The details of plants  set up so far state-wise, is \nenclosed as Annexure . \n…2 \n \n\n-2- \n… \n(b) Yes, Sir. The Government has accorded ‘in princ iple’ approval of the site at \nKovvada in Srikakulam district of Andhra Pradesh to  set up six units of 1200 \nMW each, in cooperation with USA. \n \n(c) In the Integrated Energy Policy of 2006, there was no specific mention about \nimport of nuclear reactors exceeding 6000 MW capaci ty.  The policy \ndocument indeed envisaged that capacity addition in  the country will be \nsupplemented by electricity generation through Ligh t Water Reactors (LWR), \ninitially through imports of technology but with th e long-term objective of \nindigenisation.  A capacity addition of 63,000 MW from nuclear power sources \nby 2031-32 was also projected in the document.      \n \n(d) It \nis proposed to set up total of upto 40,000 MW of nu clear power \ncapacity based on advanced Light Water Reactor tech nologies in \ncooperation with the Russian Federation, France and  the United States \nof America. \n \n(e) The reactors with foreign cooperation are plann ed to be set up on \ntechnical cooperation basis, with shared scope of w ork. The Indian \nscope is planned to be progressively increased in s ubsequent reactors \nof each technology. Provisions for lifetime fuel su pply are planned to be \nbuilt into the commercial contracts of these reactors.\n \n \n***** \n \n  \n\nAnnexure  \n \n*Under extended shutdown for techno-economic assessment for continued operation. \n** Expected to be in commercial operation by the end of this year.  \n***** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nState Location Units Capacity (MW) \nMaharashtra Tarapur \nTAPS-1 160 \nTAPS-2 160 \nTAPS-3 540 \nTAPS-4 540 \nRajasthan Rawatbhata \n RAPS-1* 100 \nRAPS-2 200 \nRAPP-3 220 \nRAPS-4 220 \nRAPS-5 220 \nRAPS-6 220 \nTamil Nadu \nKalpakkam MAPS-1 220 \nMAPS-2 220 \nKudankulam KKNPP-1 1000 \nKKNPP-2**  1000 \nUttar Pradesh Narora NAPS-1 220 \nNAPS-2 220 \nGujarat Kakrapar KAPS-1 220 \nKAPS-2 220 \nKarnataka Kaiga \nKGS-1 220 \nKGS-2 220 \nKGS-3 220 \nKGS-4 220 ",
    "ls|LS16_S10_U_108": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \n \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING & URBAN POVERTY ALLEVIATION \n \nLOK  SABHA  \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION  NO. 108 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON NOVEMBER 16, 2016 \n \nPRADHANJ MANTRI AWAS YOJANA \n \nNo. 108 SHRI DHANANJAY MADHADIK: \n  SHRIMATI SUPRIYA SULE: \n  KUNWAR BHARATENDRA: \n  SHRI BHARIO PRASAD MISHRA: \n  SHRI MOHITE PATIL VIJAYASINH SHANKARRAO: \n  SHRI SATAV RAJEEV: \n  DR. HEEN VIJAYKUMAR GAVIT: \n  DR. J. JAYAVARDHAN: \n  SHRI BADRUDDIN AJMAL: \n \nWill the Minister of HOUS ING AND URBAN POVERTY \nALLEVIATION be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the total investment made and number of houses constructed so \nfar in the Country under Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (PMAY) \nspecially in Uttar Pradesh and the details thereof;  \n \n(b) whether the Government has approved an additional investment \nfor construction of affordable ho uses for urban poor under the \nPMRAY during the first four months fo r this financial year and if so, \nthe details theroef;  \n(c) the number of urban poor who will be benefited along with the \nname of the States that will receive these funds;  \n \n(d) whether the Government has appr oved for construction of these \nhouses under three components of the urban hous ing mission and if \nso, the details thereof; and  \n \n(e) the details of other steps taken  by the Government to provide \naffordable houses to all urban poor  in the country in a time bound \nmanner? \n\nContd... \n-2- \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOUSING & URBAN \nPOVERTY ALLEVIATION \n(RAO INDERJIT SINGH) \n**** \n \n(a):  As on 10.11.2016, central assistance of Rs. 6172.03 crores \nhave been released and total 48, 236 houses have been constructed \nacross the country under all verti cals of PMAY (U) Mission including \nRajiv Awas Yojana (RAY) which has been subsumed under PMAY \n(U).  State-wise details are attached at Annexure-1.   \nNo project proposals have so far been received in this Ministry from \nthe State Government of Uttar Pradesh under centrally sponsored \ncomponents of the PMAY (U) Mission.  However, central assistance \nof Rs. 136.56 crores ha ve been released and 3,033 houses have \nbeen constructed under central sect or component vi z. Credit Link \nSubsidy Scheme (CLSS) & RAY in the State of Uttar Pradesh.   \n \n(b) & (c): During first four mont hs of the FY 2016-17, central share \nof Rs. 3693.91 crores have been accepted for construction of \n247,066 houses under all verticals of the PMAY (U) Mission.  State-\nwise details are attached at Annexure-2. \n \n(d): As on 10.11.2016, central assistance of Rs. 3,749.43 crores \nhave been accepted for construction of 10,71,869 houses across the \ncountry under the three vertical s, excluding Credit Linked Subsidy \nScheme (CLSS) componen t, of the PMAY (U) Mission.  State-wise \ndetails are at Annexure-3. \n \n \nContd... ",
