    "ls|LS16_S10_U_63": "LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 63 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 21.11.2016 \n \nJAGDISHPUR-HALDIA GAS PIPELINE PROJECT  \n \n* 63.     KUNWAR BHARATENDRA:   \n             SHRI MOHITE PATIL VIJAYSINH SHANKARRAO: \n      \n \nWill the Minister of PETROLEUM AND NATURAL GAS be pleased to state: \n \nisVªksfy;e vkSj izkd`frd xSl ea=h \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to finance the gas grid network from Jagdishpur -Haldia-\nBokaro-Dhamra gas pipeline project to push gas supply to eastern region, if so, the details \nthereof;  \n \n(b) the benefits likely to accrue to various States therefrom along with the details of funds made \navailable and utilised for laying the said gas pipeline Project, agency and State/UT-wise;  \n \n(c) whether the said project proposes to connect the eastern part of the country with the National \nGas Grid network and if so, the details thereof and the time by which the work on the said gas \npipeline is likely to be started; and  \n \n(d) the status of the project along with the further steps taken to expedite the execution of the \nproject? \nANSWER \n \nपेट्रोलियम और प्राकृलिक गैस मंत्रािय में राज् य मंत्ररी (स् विंत्र प्राार  \n(श्ररी धमेन्‍द र प्रधान  \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) IN THE MINISTRY OF \nPETROLEUM & NATURAL GAS (SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n \n(a) to (d): A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) to (d) OF THE LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 63 ASKED BY KUNWAR BHARATENDRA AND SHRI \nMOHITE PATIL VIJAYSINH SHANKARRAO,  MPs TO BE ANSWERED ON \nNOVEMBER 21, 2016 \n(a): Yes, Madam. The Government of India has taken a decision to provide a capital \ngrant of Rs.5176 crore (i.e. 40% of the estimated capital cost of Rs.12,940 Crore) to GAIL \nfor development of Jagdishpur -Haldia/Bokaro-Dhamra Gas Pipeline (JHBDPL) project, \npopularly known as the “Pradhan Mantri Urja Ganga” of Eastern India. This project will \nensure the availability of clean and eco -friendly fuel, i.e. natural gas to the Eastern part of the \ncountry. The approved year-wise capital grant details are as under:   \n \nYear Amount (Rs. Cr.) \n2016-17 900 \n2017-18 1200 \n2018-19 1500 \n2019-20 1576 \nTotal 5176 \n \n(b): JHBDPL will ensure the supply of Natural Gas to the industrial, commercial, domestic \nand transport sectors in the States of Uttar Pradesh, Bihar, Jharkhand, Odisha and West \nBengal. The details of the districts and the villages of these States to be covered by JHBDPL \nproject are as under: \n \nState Districts \ncovered \nVillages \ncovered \nPipeline \nlength \n(Km) \nAnticipated \nCost \n(Rs. Cr.) \nUttar Pradesh 8 402 342  1200  \nBihar 9 439 441  2200 \nJharkhand 11 339 524  2540 \nOdisha 13 568 762  4000 \nWest Bengal 8 523 550  3000 \nTotal 49 2270 2619  ~ 12,940   \n \nThis Capital Grant will encourage the supply of eco -friendly fuel at affordable tariffs to \nindustries and will encourage industrial development in these states. Further, GoI has decided \nsimultaneous development of City Gas Distribution (CGD) networks in ci ties namely \nVaranasi, Patna, Ranchi, Jamshedpur, Bhubaneswar, Kolkata, Cuttack etc. en -route of the \nproject. It will bring clean cooking fuel at the door step of Domestic households as well as \nprovide clean fuel to transport sector in the eastern region.  Government had earlier approved \nrevival of three Fertilizer Units (i.e. FCIL - Gorakhpur, HFCL - Barauni and FCIL -Sindri) \nalong the route of this pipeline project. On revival, these units will be the major gas customers \nfor this pipeline project. GAIL is the project implementing agency of this pipeline project and \nthe Capital Grant of Rs 5,176 Crore  will be provided to GAIL only. This Grant  will be met \nthrough the Cess collection under the Oil Industry Development Act, 1974.  So far GAIL has \n\nmade the financial commitment of Rs.1493 crore for the development of JHBDPL project in \nthe State of Uttar Pradesh and Bihar.  \n(c): Yes Madam, the JHBDPL project would connect the eastern part of the country with \nthe National Gas Grid.  GAIL has already co mmenced the construction activity in the State of \nBihar (Patna & Barauni Section) on September 15, 2015. The entire pipeline project is \nscheduled to be completed by December, 2020.  \n \n(d): This project implementing agency, i.e. GAIL has completed the survey  work for the \nentire project. In order to acquire the Right of User (RoU) land for pipeline development in \nthe State of Uttar Pradesh and Bihar, Government has published the notification for about 755 \nKm under Section 3(i) and 425 Km under Section 6(i) und er Petroleum & Mineral Pipelines \n(PMP) Act, 1962. Awards for all major supplies (line pipes, line material etc.) and laying \nworks for Phulpur to Dobhi(Gaya) and Dobhi to Patna/Barauni section  completed. GAIL \ncommenced the construction work on 15 th September 2015 on Patna & Barauni Section in the \nState of Bihar. About 41 km welding work and 19 km of pipeline lowering work completed so \nfar in this section. Further, the construction work in the State of Uttar Pradesh has also been \ncommenced on 24 th October 20 16. On the same day, Hon’ble Prime Minister laid the \nfoundation stone for the development of Varanasi City Gas Distribution (CGD) network \nwhich will enable the supply of natural gas to the domestic households, industrial & \ncommercial premises as well as Co mpressed Natural Gas (CNG) for Transport sector in \nVaranasi.  \n \n \n \n \n***** \n \n  \n\n ",
    "ls|LS16_S10_U_64": "O.I.H. \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF URBAN DEVELOPMENT \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.64 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON NOVEMBER 16, 2016 \nDANGEROUS GOVERNMENT QUARTERS \n \nNo. 64   SHRI HARINARAYAN RAJBHAR: \n \nWill the Minister of URBAN DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Central Public Works Department (CPWD) has \ndeclared a number of Government \nquarters/residences/bungalows/flats as dangerous;   \n(b) if so, the details thereof State-wise including Uttar Pradesh; \n(c) the reasons for the poor maintenance of these Government flats; \nand \n(d) the steps taken by the Government to renovate these \nGovernment residences in a phased manner? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF URBAN DEVELOPMENT \n(RAO INDERJIT SINGH) \n \n(a) & (b):  Yes, Madam.  State-wise details are annexed. \n \n(c) & (d):  Most of the flats are very old and require extensive repairs.  \nQuarters are renovated in a phased manner wherever \nfeasible.  Some colonies are taken up for redevelopment.               \n   \n****** \n  \n\nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (B) OF LOK \nSABHA UNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 64 FOR 16.11.2016 \nREGARDING “DANGEROUS GOVERNMENT QUARTERS”. \n \nSTATE WISE DETAILS OF QUARTERS/ RESIDENCES / \nBUNGALOWS / FLATS DECLARED AS DANGEROUS BY CPWD \n \nSl.No. Name of States No. of Govt. Quarters/Bungalows \netc. \n1 Delhi 1228 \n2 Maharashtra 660 \n3 Tamil Nadu 52 \n4  Goa 40 \n5 Madhya Pradesh 10 \n6 Himachal Pradesh 36 \n7 Chandigarh 02 \n8. Gujarat 100  \nIn addition 6 class rooms, 3 labs \nand 12 single room of 80 bedded \ngirls dormitory at Roop Nagar, \nBharuch) \n9. West Bengal  40 \n10. Uttar Pradesh Nil \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S10_U_65": "  GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF LAW AND JUSTICE \nLEGISLATIVE DEPARTMENT \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 65 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON WEDNESDAY, 16th NOVEMBER, 2016 \n \nVOTING OPTION BY NRIs \n \n65. SHRI RAJESHBHAI CHUDASAMA \n \n   Will the Minister of LAW AND JUSTICE be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has finalised the system to cast vote through voting \noption by Non-Resident Indian (NRI) voters; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and \n(c) the time by which is likely to be implemented/notified? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR LAW AND JUSTICE AND ELECTRONICS \nAND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n(SHRI P.P.CHAUDHARY) \n \n(a)to ( c) At present, under the provisions of section 20A of the Representation \nof the People Act, 1950 read with the Conduct of Election Rules, 1961, NRI \nvoters can cast their vote in person in the constituency where their names are \nregistered. However, b ased on the recommendation of the Election \nCommission, a proposal is under consideration of the Government to introduce \nproxy voting and postal ballot including e -postal ballot system for overseas \nelectors. e -Postal ballot  envisages transmission of blank postal ballot paper \nelectronically and thereafter return of the same by post. ",
    "ls|LS16_S10_U_66": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nDEPARTMENT OF ATOMIC ENERGY \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 66 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 16.11.2016 \n \nPRODUCTION OF ATOMIC ENERGY  \n \n66. DR. RAMESH POKHRIYAL \"NISHANK\": \n SHRI KAUSHALENDRA KUMAR:  \n \nWill the PRIME MINISTER be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the current production of Atomic energy in the country and the target fixed therefor \nfor the next ten years; \n  \n(b) whether it is more economical in comparison to other power/energy and if so, the \ndetails thereof; \n \n(c) the strategy adopted to ensure the safety and s ecurity of the Atomic energy stations; \n \n(d) the countries with which agreements have been c oncluded to boost research and \ndevelopment in the field of Atomic energy; and \n \n(e) the steps taken to promote capacity building an d skill development in the field of \nAtomic technology in the country? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR PERSONNEL, PUBLIC GRIEVANCES & PENSIONS AND \nPRIME MINISTER’S OFFICE (Dr. JITENDRA SINGH): \n \n(a) The generation of electricity from nuclear powe r in the current year (2016-17) upto \nOctober 2016 has been 22347 MUs. The target for the  current year is 36000 MU. \nTargets for generation are finalised on an annual b asis. So the targets for next ten \nyears have not been fixed. \n \n(b) Nuclear power tariffs in India are comparable t o those of other contemporary base \nload electricity generating plants. \n \n(c) Nuclear power plants are sited, designed, const ructed and operated to the highest \nsafety standards. Nuclear power plants are designed using principles of redundancy, \ndiversity and adopting a defence-in-depth approach,  constructed to highest quality \nstandards and operated strictly in line with approv ed procedures by trained and \nlicensed personnel. There is also a robust regulato ry mechanism in place. The \noverall philosophy of security and the principles a nd procedures governing the \nfunctioning of the security units in nuclear power plants are laid down in the AERB \nmanual on nuclear security. The security surveillan ce / monitoring at the nuclear \npower plant stations in the country is carried out by the Central Industrial Security \nForce (CISF). \n \n (d) Some of the major countries with which agreeme nts have been concluded to boost \nresearch and development in the field of Atomic Ene rgy are USA, Russia, France, \nUK, Australia, Republic of Korea, Canada and Czech Republic. \n \n \n(e) DAE has established dedicated multi-discipline capacity building and skill \ndevelopment centers at multiple locations in the fi eld of nuclear science and \ntechnology.  \n***** ",
    "ls|LS16_S10_U_67": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION  NO. 67 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 16.11.2016 \n \nNARROW GAUGE LINES \n \n67.  SHRIMATI RAKSHATAI KHADSE: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to at least do the regular \nmaintenance of the locomotive, coaches and track so as to \nrender the services keeping in view the safety issue and if \nso, the details thereof;  \n \n(b) whether the Government proposes to convert these narrow \ngauge lines to broad gauge; and    \n \n(c) i f so, the time bound programme chalked out in this regard \nincluding for Pachora - Jamner in Central Railway, Mumbai \nZone? \n \n ANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n       (SHRI RAJEN GOHAIN) \n \n(a)  Yes, Madam.  \n(i) Regular preventive maintenance is carried out for \nrendering satisfactory service of diesel locomotives to \nensure safe train operation.  \n(ii)  Regular maintenance of all the coaches (including Narrow \nGauge coaches) is done as per the prescribed schedules \nkeeping in view the safety and passenger amenities. \n.…2/- \n \n\n: 2 : \n \n(iii) Maintenance of track is a regular activity.  Maintenance \nand  inspection of track is done as per laid down \nprocedures.  The defects noticed during inspections get \nrectified in the planned manner.  If considered necessary, \nsuitable speed restrictions are imposed by field officials \ntill rectification of defect is done. \n \n(b) Conversion of Narrow Gauge (NG) lines, wherever feasible, \nand of Meter Gauge (MG) lines to Broad Gauge (BG) ha s been \ntaken up by Indian Railways, as a part of Uni -gauge policy in \nphases, depending on overall availability of funds and relative \npriority of the route. \n \n(c)   Survey for Gauge Conversion of Pachora -Jamner line and \nextension to Malkapur (104 Km) has been included in Rail \nBudget 2016-17 and survey taken up by Central Railway. \n \n               ***** \n \n \n \n \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S10_U_68": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n \nLOK  SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 68 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 16.11.2016 \n \n \nCONSTRUCTION OF NEW RAILWAY LINES \n \n \n68.      SHRI DEVUSINH CHAUHAN: \n                     \n  Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state:   \n \n \n(a) whether the Railways has received proposals from the \nGovernment of Gujarat for construction of new railway lines, \ngauge conversion of the existing lines and doubling of tracks to \ncope with the movement of goods from ports and industrial \ntownships to the large hinterland; and  \n \n(b) if so, the action taken so far to implement the sanctioned work, \nif any, and towards sanctioning of remaining work, proposal -\nwise?    \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI RAJEN GOHAIN) \n \n \n(a) & (b): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n*****    \n \n \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) & (b) OF \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 68 BY SHRI DEVUSINH CHAUHAN  TO \nBE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 16.11.2016 REGARDING \nCONSTRUCTION OF NEW RAILWAY LINES  \n \n(a) & (b): Requests for new lines, gauge conversion and doubling, \nboth formal as well as informal, are received by Railways at various \nlevels i.e. Railway Board, Zonal Railways and Divisional \nHeadquarters, etc. As receipt of such requests/suggestions is a \ncontinuous and dynamic process, centralized compendium of such \nrequests is not maintained. However, in recent past Government of \nGujarat has suggested certain works, the details of which are \nappended. \n \nTwo new lines, eight gauge conversion and nine doubling  \nprojects covering a length of 363 km., 1467 km and 984 km and \ncosting ` 3766 crore, ` 6510 crore and ` 6477 crore respectively \nfalling fully/partly in the State of Gujarat have been sanctioned \nwhich also will help in development of ports and industries. O n \nthese projects, an expenditure of ` 4359.47 crore has been incurred \nupto March, 201 6, with an outlay of ` 3670 crore for the yea r 2016-\n17. Besides these projects, Bhimnath-Dholera (28 km)  new line \nproject has also been included in the Budget 2016 -17 subj ect to \nrequisite approvals from the Government.      \n \nCompletion of these projects is dependent upon many factor s such \nas land acquisition, statutory clearances like forestry and wild life \nclearances, shifting of services, cutting of trees, construction of  \nroad over bridges and road under bridges by road maintaining \nagencies, apart from availability of adequate funds. Since many of \nthese factors are beyond the control of Ministry of Railways, \ntimelines for completion of all the projects are not feasible to be \nfixed.  \n***** \n \n\n \nAPPENDIX REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) & (b) OF UNSTARRED \nQUESTON NO. 68 BY SHRI DEVUSINH CHAUHAN  TO BE ANSWERED IN \nLOK SABHA ON 16.11.2016 REGARDING CONSTRUCTION OF NEW \nRAILWAY LINES  \n \n(a)  & (b):  Details and status of works suggested  by Government of \nGujarat in the recent past are as under:   \n \nS.No. Subject Status \n  New Line   \n1 Provision of \nadequate funds for \nnew line between \nSomnath to Kodinar \nfor development of \nChhara Port \nSomnath to Kodinar new line has been added \nto Rajkot - Veraval gauge conversion project \nas material modification. The main project of \ngauge conversion has already been \ncompleted. An outlay of ` 50 crore has been \nprovided for this project for the year 201 6-\n17. Land acquisition has been taken up. \nTender for major bridges is under \nfinalisation. The allotment of funds for the \nyear 2016-17  is  sufficient in present stage \nof land acquisition for the project.  \n2 New Railway line \nBhavnagar-Adhelai-\nDholera-Vataman-\nPetland (Survey \nproposed)  \n Bhavnagar-Adhelai-Dholera-Vataman-\nPetland: Survey for Bhavnagar to Tarapur \nNew Line via Dholera, has been completed. \nCost of this line has been assessed as ` 745 \ncrores with RoR of ( -) 1% and Planning \nCommission has not agreed to the proposal. \n3 Dholera-Bhimnath \n(Survey proposed)  \nThe work included in the Budget 2016 -17 \nsubject to requisite approvals from the \nGovernment.   \n4 Khambhat to \nKhambhat Port \n(Survey proposed)  \nKhambhat to Khambhat Port:  Survey for this \n20 Km line was sanctioned in 2013 -14 but \nGujarat Maritime Board has info rmed that \nKhambhat port will not be developed due to \nthe construction of Kalpsar Dam at location \nof Khambhat Port.  \n \n…..2/- \n \n\n-2- \n \n  Gauge Conversion   \n1. Gauge conversion \nof existing MG/NG \nrail line \nAhmedabad-Botad-\nBhavnagar. \nBotad-Bhavnagar is already a  broad gauge \nsection. Gauge conversion of Ahmedabad -\nBotad has been taken up at an anticipated \ncost of ` 567 crores. An expenditure of          \n` 75 crore has been incurred upto March, \n2016. An outlay of ` 102 crore has been \nprovided for this project for th e year 201 6-\n17. Final Location Survey , earthwork, \nbridges work and station building work have \nbeen taken up.    \n Doubling   \n1 Bhruch-Samni-\nDahej \nGauge conversion of this section has been \ncompleted and commissioned. At present, \nthere is no proposal for do ubling of this \nsection.  \n2 Surendranagar-\nBotad-Dhasa-\nRajula-Pipavav \nSurvey for this project has not been \nsanctioned.   \n3. Surendranagar-\nViramgam-Mehsana \n  \n(a) Doubling of Viramgam -Surendrangar (65 \nKm) section has been completed and \ncommissioned in 2015.  \n \n(b) Viramgam - Mahesana: No survey for \ndoubling of this section has been taken up. \n4. Palanpur-Bhildi-\nSamkhiali-\nGandhidham-\nMundra (Survey \ncompleted) \nPalanpur-Bhildi-Samakhiali-Gandhidham-\nMundra: On this route, (a) Doubling of \nPalanpur- Bhildi- Samakhyali has been taken \nup at an anticipated cost of ` 1267 crore \nbeing funded by Kutch Railway Company Ltd. \nAn outlay of ` 151 crore has been provided \nfor the year 201 6-17. Final location survey, \nbridges work and Road Under Bridges (RUB) \nwork have been taken up.    \n \n…3/- \n \n \n \n\n-3- \n \n  \n \n(b) Samakhayali - Gandhidham-Adipur is \nalready an existing double broad gauge line \nsection.  \n \n(c) No survey for doubling of Adipur - Mundra \nhas been sanctioned. \n5 Viramgam-\nSamakhaili-\nGandhidham \n(proposed to be \ntaken up in 2011 -\n12)  \nViramgam-Samakhaili-Gandhidham: \nViramgam-Sadla (21 km) , Jatpipli-Vasadva \n(12 km) & Chuli -Sukhpur (10 km) sections \nhave been completed & commissioned. \nWorks in balance section have been taken \nup.  \nSamakhayali-Gandhidham is already an \nexisting double line section. \n6 \n \nAhmedabad-\nMehsana-Jaipur \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n(a) The work of Gauge conversion of \nAhmedabad-Mehsana (70 km) metre gauge \n(MG) line running parallel to existing broad \ngauge (BG) line has been included in the \nBudget 2015-16. Detailed estimate has been \nsanctioned. Tendering for earthwork bridges \nwork, ballast supply, track linking have been \ntaken up.   \n(b)   Survey for Doubling of Mehsana - \nPalanpur (65 Km) section has been taken up.  \n(c)    Doubling of Palanpur -Ajmer has been \nsanctioned in different patches and works \nhave been taken up.  \n(d)   Ajmer-Jaipur is already a double line \nsection. \n \n \n7  Rajkot-Veraval  Rajkot-Veraval doubling surveys (in 2 parts) \nhave been taken up.  \n \n8 Rajkot-Okha  Survey has been taken up. \n \n….4/-  \n \n\n-4- \n \n9  Rajkot-Viramgam   (a)    Doubling of Surendranagar -Rajkot (116 \nkm) has been included in the Budget 2015 -\n16. Detailed estimate has been sanctioned. \nTender for final location survey, earthwork, \nbridges work and ballast supply have been \ninvited.  \n   \n(b) Doubling of Viramgam -Surendrangar (65 \nKm) section has been completed and \ncommissioned in 2015.  \n \n \n****** \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S10_U_69": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF TOURISM \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.*69 \nANSWERED ON 21.11.2016 \n \nPROMOTION OF WILDLIFE AND FOREST TOURISM  \n \n*69. SHRI RAMDAS C. TADAS:  \nSHRI NANA PATOLE:  \n \nWill the Minister of TOURISM be pleased to state:  \n \n(a)  whether th e Government plans to develop wildlife and forest \ntourism in the country, if so, the details thereof along with its \nscope in various States, State/UT-wise including Maharashtra;  \n(b)  whether the Government has received any proposals in this \nregard from th e various State Governments or public \nrepresentatives and if so, the details thereof and the status of \nthe said proposals;  \n(c)  the funds allocated for the purpose during the last three years \nand the current year, year-wise;  \n(d)  the other steps taken by  the Government to develop these \nforests as tourist sites; and  \n(e)  the time by which these places are likely to be developed \nunder wildlife and forest tourism?  \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR TOURISM (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)  \n(DR. MAHESH SHARMA) \n \n(a)  to (e): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.  \n \n \n******** \n\nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO.*69 \nANSWERED ON 21.11.2016 REGARING PROMOTION OF WILDLIFE \nAND FOREST TOURISM. \n \n(a) to (d): India has huge tourism potential including wildlife an d \nforest tourism in the country including in the State of Maharashtra. \nDevelopment and promotion of tourist destinations and products \nincluding Wildlife & Forest Tourism is primarily the responsibility of \nthe respective State Government/Union Territory (UT ) \nAdministration. \n \nHowever, for development of tourism infrastructure in the \ncountry, the Ministry of Tourism has launched the Swadesh Darshan \nscheme- Integrated Development of Theme -Based Tourist Circuits, \nin 2014-15.  \n \nWildlife Circuit has been identifie d as one of the thirteen \nthematic circuits for development under this operative scheme.  \n \nThe Ministry has sanctioned following projects in the year \n2015-16 for the Wildlife Circuit under Swadesh Darshan scheme:  \n \nState Name of Project Amount \nSanctioned \n(Rs. in Crore) \nMadhya \nPradesh \nDevelopment of Wildlife Circuit at Panna - \nMukundpur- Sanjay- Dubri-Bandhavgarh-\nKanha-Mukki-Pench \n92.22 \nAssam Manas-Pobitora-Nameri-Kaziranga-Dibru-\nSaikhowa as Wildlife Circuit in Assam  \n95.67 \n \n(e): The completion period of pro jects sanctioned under the \nSwadesh Darshan scheme varies from 18 to 36 months.  \n******** ",
    "ls|LS16_S10_U_7": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 7 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 16/11/2016  \n  \nVULGARTITY IN TV PROGRAMME \n \n*7.  SHRI  JANARDAN SINGH SIGHRIWIL : \n \nWill the Minister of INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING    \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has taken cognizance ris e in  obscenity, vulgarity and \nnudity in the television programmes in the country;  \n \n(b) if so, the details of channels against whom act ion has been taken for violating the \nnorms/guidelines during the last three years and the current year; \n \n(c)  whether there is any self regulation in place to check/curb vulgarity and indecency in \nprogrammes telecast on TV channels and if so, the details in the this regard; and  \n \n(d) the steps taken/being taken by the Government t o monitor the content of the \nprogrammes being  telecast on Doordarshan and Private channels? \n  \n  \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF INFORMATION & BROADCASTING \n(SHRI M. VENKAIAH NAIDU) \n \n(a) to (d): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.  \n \n********** \n \n\n \nSTATEMENT AS REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO ( d) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 7 FOR ANSWER ON 16.11.2016  \n \n \n(a) to (d):  As per existing regulatory framework, all programmes telecast on TV \nchannels are required to adhere to the Programme Co de  prescribed  under the Cable \nTelevision Networks (Regulation) Act, 1995 and Cabl e Television Network Rules, 1994 \nframed thereunder.  The Act does not provide for pr e-censorship of any programme \ntelecast on such TV channels.  However, it prescrib es that all programmes telecast on such \nTV channels should be in conformity with the prescr ibed Programme Code enshrined in the \nsaid Act and the rules framed thereunder, which con tains a whole range of parameters to \nregulate programmes including content of obscenity,  vulgarity and nudity in TV \nprogrammes.  \n \nMinistry has constituted an Inter Ministerial Commi ttee (IMC) to look into the \nviolations suo-motu or whenever violation of the Pr ogramme and Advertising Codes is \nbrought to the notice of this Ministry in respect o f private satellite TV channels by vigilant \ncitizens about objectionable content on TV. IMC has  representatives from the Ministry of \nHome Affairs, Defence, External Affairs, Law, Women  and Child Development, Health and \nFamily Welfare, Consumer Affairs and a representati ve from the industry in Advertising \nStandards Council of India (ASCI). IMC meets period ically and recommends action in \nrespect of violations. Details of action taken on v iolation of Programme Code by private TV \nchannels for telecast of content of obscenity, vulg arity and nudity in TV programmes during \nthe last three years and the current year are enclosed at Annexure. \n \nTV channels are required to preserve a copy of thei r telecast for 90 days. In case a \nviolation is reported they are obliged to share the  recordings and archive it until the matter \nis resolved.  \n \nGovernment has encouraged self-regulation in electr onic media by the Industry. \nNews Broadcasters Association (NBA), which represen ts Private television news and \ncurrent affairs broadcasters, as part of its self-r egulation mechanism, has formulated  a  \nCode  of  Ethics  and  Broadcasting  Standards  covering  a  wide range of principles to self-\nregulate news broadcasting. NBA has also formulated  News Broadcasting Standards \nRegulations. They have set up a Two-Tier structure to deal with content related complaints- \nat Tier I, by the individual broadcasters and at Ti er II, by News Broadcasting Standards \n\nAuthority (NBSA). The Authority consists of a Chair person who is a retired Judge of the \nSupreme Court and eight other members. Members of t he Authority comprise of 4 (four) \neminent editors employed with broadcaster and 4 (fo ur) persons having special knowledge \nand/or practical experience in the field of law, ed ucation, medicine, science, literature, \npublic administration, consumer affairs, environment, human psychology and/or culture.  \n           \nBesides, Indian Broadcasting Foundation (IBF), whic h represents non-News and \nentertainment channels, has laid down Content Code & Certification Rules 2011 covering \nan entire gamut of content-related principles and c riterion for television broadcast.  As part \nof self-regulation mechanism, a two-Tier complaints  redressal system has been set up by \nIBF. At the Tier-I level, each Broadcaster has set up a Standard and Practices (S&P) \nDepartment with a Content Auditor to deal with the   complaints   received for content aired \non its channels.  At the Tier II, a Broadcast Conte nt Complaints Council (BCCC) has been \nset up. The BCCC has 13 Members headed by a retired  Judge of the Supreme Court or \nHigh Court as Chairperson and 12 other Members, viz. 4 eminent persons, 4 members from \nany National Level Statutory Commissions and 4 Broa dcast members and two (2) Special \nInvitees to deal with complaints against regional language content.  \n            \nAlso, Advertising Standards Council of India (ASCI) , established in 1985, has set up \nConsumer Complaints Council (CCC) to consider compl aints in respect of advertisements.  \nThe CCC currently has 28 members; 12 are from withi n the industry and 16 are from the \ncivil society like well known doctors, lawyers, jou rnalists, academicians, consumer activists \netc. \n        \nIn so far as Doordarshan Channels are concerned, Do ordarshan has its own \nBroadcasting Code and Social Objectives and adverti sement Code for production and \ntelecast of programmes to ensure that no programmes  containing obscenity, vulgarity and \nnudity go on air.  \n \n*********** \n\nANNEXURE  \n \nANNEURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF  LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION No.* 7 FOR ANSWRE ON 16.11.2016  \n \nAction Taken on violation of Programme and Advertis ement code by Private TV \nchannels for telecasting content depicting vulgarity, obscenity in last three years and \ncurrent year.  \nYear – 2013  \nSl. \nNo.  \nName of the \nChannel \nReason for Show Cause Notice  Details of action taken  \n1.  Enterr 10 Telecast of Hindi feature film \n'Musafir' , 'Plan'  and 'Ashiq Banaya \nApnne'-  'A' certified films. \nOrder dated 08.01.2013 was issued to \nthe channel prohibiting  the transmission \nof the channel for one day . \n2.  Zing  Telecast of Hindi feature film \n\"Hawas\" - 'A' certified film. \nOrder dated 08.01.2013 was issued to \nthe channel prohibiting  the transmission \nof the channel for one day . \n3.  Manoranjan \nTV \nTelecast of Hindi feature film \n\"Topless\" - \"A' certified film. \nOrder dated 08.01.2013 was issued to \nthe channel prohibiting the transmission \nof the channel for one day . \n4.  SS TV Telecast of Trailer of the film \n\"Friends with Benefits\" which was \nnot certified by CBFC for telecast \non TV channels. \nOrder dated 08.01.2013 was issued to \nthe channel prohibiting the transmission \nof the channel for one day . \n5.  FTV Telecast of an advertisement of \nVodka on 2.3.2011 in a programme \nFashion TV Launch Party \n \nAn Advisory dated 17.01.2013 was  \nissued to the channel. \n6.  FTV  Telecast of programme \"Desigers \nin High Definition\" on 11.9.11, \n\"Chantellie Lingrie, Paris\" on \n12.09.11 & \"Lingerie\" on 15.09.11 \nand \"15th Anniversary-Top \nDesigners\" showing obscene and \nwomen denigrating content \nAn Order dated 28.03.2013 was issued \nto the channel prohibiting the \ntransmission of the channel for 10 days  \n7.  NDTV Good \nTimes \nTelecast of programme \"Life a \nBeach\" during April, May ,2011 \nshowing obscene and women \ndenigrating content \nAn Advisory dated 02.04.2013 was \nissued to the channel. \n8.  Mahuaa Telecast of Hindi feature film \n'Aulaad' and 'Ek Aur Kurukshetra' -   \n'A' certified films. \nAn order dated 25.04.2013 was issued to \nthe channel  prohibiting the transmission \nof the channel for one day. \n9.  AXN Telecast of Hindi feature film \n'Darkness Falls' -  'A' certified film. \nAn order dated 25.04.2013 was issued to \nthe channel  prohibiting the transmission \nof the channel for one day. \n10.  Movies Ok Telecast of Hindi feature film 'Dil \nJale' -  'A' certified film. \nAn order dated 01.05.2013 was issued to \nthe channel  prohibiting the transmission \nof the channel for one day. \n11.  Comedy \nCentral \nTelecast of programme \"Stand Up \nClub\" \nAn order was issued on 17.05.2013 \nprohibiting the transmission of the \nchannel for 10 days  \n12.  IBN 7 Telecast of the Advertisement of \n\"Axe Shower Gel\" containing vulgar \nand indecent content. \nOrder dated 29.05.2013 was issued \ndirecting the channel to furnish an \nundertaking regarding not airing such \nads in future. \n13.  MTV Telecast of the advertisement of \n\"Axe Shower Gel\" containing vulgar \nand indecent content. \nOrder dated 17.06.2013 was issued \ndirecting the channel to furnish an \nundertaking regarding not airing such \nads in future. \n\n14.  VH1 Telecast of advertisement of \"Axe \nShower Gel\" showing obscene and \nwomen denigrating content \nOrder dated 17.06.2013 was issued \ndirecting the channel to furnish an \nundertaking regarding not airing such \nads in future. \n15.  Colors Telecast of advertisement of \"Axe \nShower Gel\" showing obscene and \nwomen denigrating content \nOrder dated 17.06.2013 was issued \ndirecting the channel to furnish an \nundertaking regarding not airing such \nads in future. \n16.  N TV Telecast of  News report showing \ncontents offending good taste and \ndecency and women denigrating \nAn order dated 18.09.13 issued to the \nchannel to run the  apology scroll  for \nthree days. \n17.  Zoom TV Telecast of Film \"Teesri Aankh - 'A' \ncertified film. \nAn order dated 01.10.2013 was issued  \nto prohibit the transmission or re-\ntransmission  for one day \n18.  ABN Andhra \nJyoti \nTelecast of a song based \nprogramme on       \"Ide Mallea \nVelavani\" containing obscene and \nwomen denigrating content \nAn order dated 01.10.2013 was issued to \nthe channel to prohibit the transmission \nor re-transmission for seven days. \n19.  Manoranjan \nTV \nTelecast of 'A' Certified Hindi \nfeature film \"Ek Chatur Nar\" \norder was issued on 17.05.2013 to \nprohibit the transmission or re-\ntransmission of channel for seven days \n20.  BIG CBS \nLOVE \nTelecast of programme \"Excused\" \ncontaining women denigrating \ncontent \nAn order was issued on 15.10.2013 to \nthe channel to prohibit the transmission \nor re-transmission of  channel for one \nday.  \n21.  UTV Bindass  Telecast of  a programme \n\"Emotional Atyachaar Season 3\" \ncontaining obscene content \nAn order dated 06.11.2013 was issued to \nprohibit the transmission or re-\ntransmission  for three days \n22.  Manoranjan \nTV \nTelecast of various films without \nshowing CBFC certificates \nA warning dated 26.12.2013 was issued \nto the channel \n \n  \n \nYear – 2014  \n \nSl. \nNo.  \nName of the \nChannel \nReason for Show Cause Notice  Details of action taken  \n \n23.  WB Telecast of a  \"V/UA\" certified film \n\"It's a Boy Girl Thing\" showing \nobscene and women denigrating \ncontent \nOrder dated 16.01.2014 was issued  for \ntaking the channel off air for one day.  \n24.  Lemon News Telecast a news report, revealing the \nidentity of the sexually abused \nwomen \nA warning dated 10.03.2014 was issued \nto channel \n25.  Amrita TV Telecast of 'A' Certified film, 'The \nDon' \nA warning dated 27.03.2014 was issued \nto channel \n26.  All channels TV Channels continue Telecast \nFilms without displaying CBFC \nCertificates. \nA Advisory dated 29.05.2014 was issued \nto All TV Channels. \n27.  Vasanth TV Telecast a programme called \n'Vaimaye Vellum' revealed the \nidentity of  sexually abused minor \nchildren \nA warning dated 27.08.2014 was issued \nto the channel  \n \n \n \n \n\nYear – 2015  \n \nSl. \nNo.  \nName of the \nChannel \nReason for Show Cause Noti ce  Details of action taken  \n \n28. NTV  Telecast a song-based programme \n'Cine Colors' \nAn order dated 19.01.2015 was issued to \nthe channel for taking the channel off air \nfor seven day.  \n29. NTV Telecast of news report revealed the \nidentity of sexual harassment  minor \nboy \nAn Warning dated 23.03.2015 was \nissued to channel  \n30. Satlon News Telecast of News report about a \nprivate corporate party organised in \na five star hotel on the Pune-Mumbai \nhighway \nAn order was issued on 27.03.2015 to \nthe channel to prohibit the transmission \nor re-transmission of  channel for 30 day. \n \n31.  Jai Hind Telecast of 'A; certified film, titled \n'Hai Harithe' \nAn order was issued on 07.04.2015 to \nthe channel to prohibit the transmission \nor re-transmission of  channel for one \nday.  \n32.  Russia Today \nTV \nTelecast of obscene programme \n'Crazy Alert'  \nAn Advisory dated 06.07.2015 was \nissued the channel. \n33.  A2Z News \nTV \nThe Channel telecast news reports \non various date and revealed the \nidentity of Sexual assault minor \nvictims  \nA warning dated 07.08.2015 was issued \nto the channel. \n \nYEAR- 2016 \n \nSl. \nNo.  \nName of the \nChannel \nReason for Show Cause Notice  Details of action taken  \n \n34.  Care World Telecast of a programme \"Kya Karun \nMain AB?\" on unnatural sex. \nA warning dated 24.05.2016 was issued \nto the channel. \n35.  F TV Telecast of a programme namely \nfotos in alleged violation of the \nprogramme code \nAn Advisory dated 25.05.2016 issued to \nthe channel \n36.  CVR English \nNews \nChannel \nTelecast of  News bulletins showing \ndisturbing visuals of dead bodies \nAn Advisory dated 25.05.2016 issued to \nthe channel \n37.  Oscar Movies  Telecast of 'A' certified films on \nvarious dates. \nAn Advisory dated 06.06.2016 issued to \nthe channel \n38. Care World Telecast obscene programme 'Kya \nKaru Mai Aab \nAn order was issued on 02.11.2016 to \nthe channel to prohibit the transmission \nor re-transmission of  channel for one \nday \n39 News Time \nAssam \nTelecast of News story  defaming the \nimage of MLA and denigrating \nwomen \nAn order dated 2.11.2016 \nwas issued on  \n2.11.2016 to the channel to prohibit the \ntransmission or re-transmission of \nchannel for one day ( carry out the three \nawards of one day off air concurrently \n \n***** ",
    "ls|LS16_S10_U_70": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMIINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 70 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 16.11.2016 \n \n   CHARGES FOR USING URINALS \n \n70.    DR. KIRIT SOMAIYA: \n      Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)   whether a charge of Re.1 has been imposed to use urinals in Mulund \nand other railway stations in Mumbai suburban railways;  \n \n(b)     if so, the details and reasons therefor;  \n \n(c)    whether the Government is aware that commuters have raised strong \nobjections against this charge and has demanded its withdrawal;  \n \n(d)    if so, whether the Railways will consider to withdraw this charge; and \n \n(e)    if not, the reasons therefor? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n(SHRI RAJEN GOHAIN) \n \n(a) to (b):  Yes, Madam.  A charge of `1 has been imposed to use urinals in \n‘Pay & Use’ toilets at Mulund and other suburban railway stations  in \nMumbai in order to provide better and hygienic services at sub urban \nstations having high foot fall.  However, for toilet b locks which are \nmaintained departmentally, there is no usage charge. \n \n(c): Amongst 22 stations where urinals are being charged at  `1, \ncomplaints have been received for 3 stations namely Mumbai CST, Mulund \nand Shahad station. \n \n(d) & (e) : As per extant polic y guidelines of Zonal Railway, urinals are \nbeing charged for `1 at Mumbai suburban railway stations. No such \nproposal for revision of policy guidelines is in pipeline at present.  \n****** \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S10_U_71": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF COMMERCE & INDUSTRY \nDEPARTMENT OF INDUSTRIAL POLICY & PROMOTION \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 71. \nTO BE ANSWERED ON MONDAY, THE 21ST NOVEMBER,  2016. \n \nDEVELOPMENT OF SALT INDUSTRY \n \n*71.  SHRI KUNDARIYA MOHAN BHAI KALYANJI BHAI: \n \nWill the Minister of COMMERCE AND INDUSTRY be pleased to state: \n                            वाणिज्‍ य‍वव ‍द्यग ‍ं ्री \n(a)  whether meetings were held between  Government of Gujarat and Union  \nGovernment in 2012, in connection with  development of salt industry and \nagarias in the State and if so, the outcome of the meetings; \n \n(b)  the action taken/being taken to  reimburse the State Government the  \nexpenditure incurred on development of  salt industry schemes/projects and \nwelfare schemes for the salt workers; and \n \n(c)  whether the Union Government  proposes to contribute 50 per cent amount  of \nthe State Salt Projects so that more  projects and better activities are taken up  \nin Gujarat and if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nवाणिज्‍ य‍वव ‍द्यग ‍ााज्‍ यं ्री‍स्‍‍ वतं ्‍्रभााा(स्रींतंरी‍िरंमलाा‍ीरीतंाांि(‍ \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMERCE & INDUSTRY \n(SHRIMATI NIRMALA SITHARAMAN) \n \n(a): No meeting was held between Government of Gujarat and Government \nof India in 2012 regarding development of salt industry and agarias in \nthe State. \n \n(b): There is no scheme of the Government of India which envisages \nreimbursement to the State Government of the expenditure incurred on \ndevelopment of salt industry/projects and welfare schemes for salt \nworkers. \n \n(c):  No such proposal is under consideration. \n \n***** ",
    "ls|LS16_S10_U_72": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 72 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 16.11.2016 \n \nGAUGE CONVERSION \n \n \n †72.  SHRI RAHUL KASWAN: \n \n \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n \n(a)  the number of gauge conversion projects sanctioned, completed \nand lying incomplete in the country during the last three years \nalong with the complete details thereof; \n  \n(b)  the number of gauge conversion projects in the State of Rajasthan \nwhich  have been completed after sanction and those lyin g \nincomplete; \n  \n(c)  whether in this year's budget, provision had been made for the \ncompletion of gauge conversion work in the State of Rajasthan and \nif so, the details thereof, project-wise; \n  \n(d)  whether work has stated for the sanctioned amount and the time by \nwhich it will be completed; and \n  \n(e)  if so, the details thereof?  \n  \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI RAJEN GOHAIN) \n \n \n(a) to (e):   A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n***** \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO ( e) OF UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 72 BY SHRI RAHUL KASWAN TO BE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA \nON 16.11.2016 REGARDING GAUGE CONVERSION \n \n(a):   Four Gauge Conversion projects have been included in Railway Budgets \nsince 2013-14 subject to requisite approvals.  Details are as given below:- \nS. \nNo. \nRly State Project Year Length      \n(in km)  \nLatest \nCost  \nOutlay \n2016-\n17  \n(in ` Crore) \n1 NER UP Indara-Dohrighat (34 \nKm) \n2016-17 34 120 0.02 \n2 NER UP Bahraich-Mailani incl \nbyepass at Mailani \n(230 Km) \n2016-17 230 1900 0.02 \n3 WR GUJ Ahmedabad- \nMahesana (70 Km) \n2015-16 70 420 100 \n4 SECR MAH Nagbhir-Nagpur (106 \nkm) \n2013-14 106 401 25 \n \nIn three financial years starting from 2013 -14, a total of 2337 Km Gauge \nConversion has been completed.  As on date, 39 Gauge Conversion works have \nbeen taken up. \n \n(b) to (e):  One gauge conversion project viz. Suratpura-Hanumangarh (174 Km) \nhas recently been completed  falling fully/partly in the State of Rajasthan .  \nDetails of ongoing gauge conversion projects falling fully or partly in the State of \nRajasthan are as under:- \nS. \nNo. \nRly. State Project Name Year of \nSanction \nLength \n(in \nKm) \nCost  Expendi-\nture \nupto \n31.03.16 \nOutlay \n2016-\n17 \n(In ` Crores) \n1 NCR MP, \nRAJ \nGwalior-\nSheopurkalan with \nextension to Kota \n(284 km) \n2010-11 284 3845 10.46 35 \n\nS. \nNo. \nRly. State Project Name Year of \nSanction \nLength \n(in \nKm) \nCost  Expendi-\nture \nupto \n31.03.16 \nOutlay \n2016-\n17 \n(In ` Crores) \n2 NCR RAJ Dholpur-Sirmuttra \nwith extension to \nGangapur City \n(144.6 km) \n2010-11 144.6 2530 35.66 50 \n3 NWR RAJ Sadulpur-Bikaner \n& Ratangarh-\nDegana (394.35 \nkm) with \nRatangarh-\nSardarshahar (44 \nkm) sanctioned as \nMM \n2007-08 438.35 886.\n22 \n814.14 10 \n4 NWR RAJ, \nHAR \nJaipur-Ringus-\nChuru & Sikar-\nLoharu (320.04 \nkm) \n2008-09 320.04 915 453.54 100 \n5 NWR RAJ Ajmer-Chitturgarh-\nUdaipur incl MM \nUdaipur-Umra and \nMavli-Bari \nSadri(393 Km) \n1996-97 393 865 557.18 15 \n6 WR RAJ, \nGUJ \nAhmedabad-\nHimmatnagar-\nUdaipur including \nModasa-Shamlaji \nRoad(22.53Km) \n2008-09 321.73 1662 233.69 675.25 \n \nThus a total allotment of `885.25 Crore has been made for these Gauge \nConversion projects.  As  execution of a railway project  requires several \nclearances and assistance from other departments which are beyond the control \nof railways, it will not be feasible to fix time lines for completion of all the \nprojects.  \n***** ",
    "ls|LS16_S10_U_73": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 73 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 16.11.2016 \n \nHIGH SPEED RAIL PROJECT \n \n73.        SHRI A. ARUNMOZHITHEVAN: \n  \n     Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether a Joint Committee has held talks with Japanese authorities \nvery recently regarding India’s ambitious high speed rail project;  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(c) whether India has requested for drawing up of a sche dule of project \nimplementation and appointment of a General Consultant before \nfinalisation of the loan agreement for the said project; and \n \n(d) if so, the response received from the Japanese authorities in this \nregard? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI RAJEN GOHAIN) \n \n(a) & (b): Yes, Madam. Third Joint Committee meeting under the \nchairmanship of Vice Chairman, NITI Aayog was held with Japanese \ncounterpart on 7th October, 2016 to review the progress of Mumbai -\nAhmedabad High Speed Rail project.     \n \n(c) & (d) : Yes, Madam. Both Government of India and Government of \nJapan have agreed to the schedule of implementation of project and \nappointment of the General Consultant before finalisation of loan \nagreement.  \n***** ",
    "ls|LS16_S10_U_74": "1\n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF CULTURE \n \nLOK SABHA\n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n74\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON \n21.11.2016\n \nKARTIKA 30\n, 193\n8\n \n(SAKA)\n \n \n \nMAINTENANCE OF HERITAGE SITES BY PRIVATE SECTOR \n \n \n \n*74.\n \nSHRI  R. GOPALAKRISHNAN:\n \nSHRI  HARISH CHANDER \nALIAS\n  \nHARISH DWIVEDI: \n \n \nWill the Minister of CULTURE be pleased to state:\n \n \n(a)\n \nthe number of historical monuments and heritage sites maintained by the \nArchaeological Survey of India (ASI) State/UT\n-\nwise; \n \n(b)\n \nwhether heritage sites in the country are being given to private compa\nnies for \ntheir renovation and maintenance and if so, the details thereof and the reasons \ntherefor; \n \n(c)\n \nthe other steps taken by the Government to promote private sector’s \ninvolvement in heritage promotion along with the details thereof; and \n \n(d)\n \nwhether\n \nASI has undertaken responsibility of maintaining historical/heritage \nsites situated in foreign countries also and if so, the details thereof?\n \n \n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF STATE, CULTURE AND TOURISM (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)\n \n \n(DR. MAHESH SHARMA)\n \n \n \n(a)to(d)\n \nA Stateme\nnt is laid on the table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n\n2\n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) TO (\nd\n) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n74\n \nFOR \n21.11.2016\n \n \n \n(a)\n \nThe State\n-\nwise list of 3686 monuments/sites \nmaintained by the \nArchaeological Survey of India in the countr\ny \nis at Annexure. \n \n \n(b)\n \nAs on date, Archaeological Survey of India has undertaken conservation \nand development of Humayun’s Tomb, Delhi in collaboration with Aga \nKhan Trust for Culture (AKTC) and conservation and development of \nTomb of Mohammed Shah known\n \nas Mubarak Shah’s Gumbad, Delhi in \ncollaboration with Indian National Trust for Cultural Heritage (INTACH). \nFurther MOU’s have been signed with State Governments for \nmaintenance and upgrading visitor facilities.  However, in no case whole \nwork is entruste\nd to any private company. \n \n(c)\n \nArchaeological Survey of India has issued an Expression of Interest on \nPublic Private Partnership Module (PPP) for providing World class \nfacilities at the important tourist visited monuments/sites.  Under this \nExpression of \nInterest (EOI) 20 different services which includes web\n-\nbased information and other innovative ideas which enhance the \npopularity of the monument and bring it at par have been offered.  \n \n(d)\n \nOn request from MEA the ASI has taken up conservation work of Ta\n \nProhm Temple in Combodia, Vat Phom temple in Lao PDR and Anande \nTemple in Myanmar.\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n3\n \n \nANNEXURE \n \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) OF LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION \nNO. 74 FOR 21.11.2016\n \n \nNUMBER OF CENTRALLY PROTECTED MONUMENTS/SITES UNDE\nR THE JURISDICTION \nOF ARCHAEOLOGICAL SURVEY OF INDIA IN THE COUNTRY \n \n \n \nSl.No.\n \nName of State\n \nNos. of Monuments\n \n1\n.\n \n \nAndhra Pradesh\n \n129\n \n2\n.\n \n \nArunachal Pradesh\n \n03\n \n3\n.\n \n \nAssam\n \n55\n \n4\n.\n \n \nBihar\n \n70\n \n5\n.\n \n \nChhattisgarh\n \n47\n \n6\n.\n \n \nDaman & Diu (U. T.)\n \n12\n \n7\n.\n \n \nGoa\n \n21\n \n8\n.\n \n \nGujarat\n \n203\n \n9\n.\n \n \nHaryana\n \n91\n \n10\n.\n \n \nHimachal Pradesh\n \n40\n \n11\n.\n \n \nJammu & Kashmir\n \n69\n \n12\n.\n \n \nJharkhand\n \n13\n \n13\n.\n \n \nKarnataka \n \n506\n \n14\n.\n \n \nKerala\n \n28\n \n15\n.\n \n \nMadhya Pradesh\n \n292\n \n16\n.\n \n \nMaharashtra\n \n285\n \n17\n.\n \n \nManipur\n \n01\n \n18\n.\n \n \nMeghalaya\n \n08\n \n19\n.\n \n \nMizoram\n \n01\n \n20\n.\n \n \nNagaland\n \n04\n \n21\n.\n \n \nN.C.T. Delhi\n \n174\n \n22\n.\n \n \nOdisha\n \n79\n \n23\n.\n \n \nPuducherry (U.T.)\n \n07\n \n24\n.\n \n \nPunjab\n \n33\n \n25\n.\n \n \nRajastha\nn\n \n162\n \n26\n.\n \n \nSikkim\n \n03\n \n27\n.\n \n \nTelangana\n \n08\n \n28\n.\n \n \nTamil Nadu\n \n413\n \n29\n.\n \n \nTripura\n \n08\n \n30\n.\n \n \nUttar Pradesh\n \n743\n \n31\n.\n \n \nUttarakhand\n \n42\n \n32\n.\n \n \nWest Bengal\n \n \n136\n \n \nTOTAL\n \n3686\n \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S10_U_75": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED  QUESTION NO.  75  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 16.11.2016 \n  \nONGOING RAIL PROJECTS IN UP \n \n  +  75.   SHRI KAUSHAL KISHORE:     \n  \n        Will the Minister of RAILWAYS  be pleased to state t he details of \nrail projects in Uttar Pradesh through which employment \nopportunities may be/have been provided to the unemployed \nmen/women of the Scheduled Castes/Scheduled Tribes?    \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n(SHRI RAJEN GOHIN) \n    A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n***** \n  \n\nSTATEMENT R EFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART OF UNSTARRED \nQUESTION No.75  BY SHRI KAUSHAL KISHORE TO BE ANSWERED IN \nLOK SABHA ON 16.11.2016 REGARD ING ONGOING RAIL PROJECTS IN \nUP \n         Every Railway project acts as a catalyst of growth and \ndevelopment in the project area bringing several opportunities of \ndirect and  indirect employment for all sections of society including \nthose unemployed men/women belonging to SCs & STs. List of ongoing \nrailway projects falling partially/fully in UP is as under:-   \nS.No. Name of the Project Year of \ninclusion/ \nsanction \nLength   (in \nkm)  \n  NEW   LINES   \n1 Kapilvastu-Basti 2013-14 91 \n2 Anandnagar-Ghugli 2013-14 50 \n3 Chhitauni-Tumkuhi Road (58.88 km) 2006-07 62.5 \n4 Hathua-Bhatni 2005-06 79.64 \n5 Mau-Ghazipur-Tarighat  2015-16 51 \n6 Sahjanwa-Dohrighat 2016-17 70.45 \n7 Bahraich-Shravasti-\nBalrampur/Tulsipur \n2016-17 210 \n8 Faizabad-Lalganj via Raibareilly 2013-14 116 \n9 Unchhar-Amethi 2012-13 66.17 \n10 Deoband (Muzzafar Nagar)-Roorkee \n(27.45 km) \n2007-08 27.45 \n11 Meerut-Panipat 2016-17 104 \n12 Lalitpur-Satna, Rewa-Singrauli & \nMahoba-Khajuraho (541 km) \n1997-98 541 \n  GAUGE CONVERSION     \n13 Lucknow-Pilibhit via Sitapur, \nLakhimpur (262.76 km) \n2011-12 262.76 \n\n14 Bhojipura-Tanakpur via Pilibhit  2007-08 101.79 \n15 Gonda-Baharaich 1997-98 60 \n16 Indara-Dohri